.TH sway-things-hook 1 "" "Sway Things 0.3.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-hook \- Run a hook; the generated sway config runs these
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things hook\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a hook; the generated sway config runs these
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-gsettings(1)
Copy the stored settings that GTK apps read from GSettings (cursor theme and size) to GSettings; run at login and at each reload of sway
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-displays(1)
Switch a display on if none is on (and have kanshi apply its profile again, if it runs): run at every start and reload of sway while Sway Things stores anything for a display, so it never leaves you without one
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-workspaces(1)
Put the workspaces on the displays connected now as the Workspaces page says: run at every start and reload of sway while a rule places them, and by kanshi when it applied a profile
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-mirror(1)
Show displays on others as remembered for the displays connected now (wl\-mirror), and end the mirrors of other combinations: run by kanshi when it applied a profile
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-notification\-click(1)
Bring the window of a clicked notification\*(Aqs app to the front: run by swaync (as a script, with the notification in its environment) and mako (with \-\-mako) while the Notifications page says so
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-notification\-daemon(1)
Start the notification daemon chosen on the Notifications page unless one runs: run at every start and reload of sway while one is chosen
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-quick(1)
Switch Do Not Disturb, Wi\-Fi, Bluetooth, the sound or the microphone: run by the buttons of swaync\*(Aqs panel
